's been talking about it  much earlier  and when more and more people start  talking about mental health issues the  fact that they have taken help  it does have an impact we have to accept  that role models and influencers  have an immense impact especially on the  young population that that that's an  absolute fact  i think what's happening during coven is  that  an individual may not realize that they  are talking about mental health but  it is mental health that's been  addressed for example  the fear of getting an illness or the  fear of what if something happens to  your family  fear of getting treatment on time  all of these anxieties and fear and  stresses  like examinations uh results  jobs economy all of these psychosocial  factors  do give stress so when people start  talking about it  in a way that's also primary  intervention of mental health  because rather than bottling it up you  are talking about it because you realize  it's not universal right a pandemic is a  pandemic because it is pan  so now relatedness about distress  is easier so unmuting sharing  about it has become more spontaneous  and which i think is also in a way an  intervention for a country like ours  because like i've been saying  expertisation is not the solution the  strength of india always have been  in its interdependent  family system social system  so the more connected engaged  and communication that happens  in this dissociative milieu which is the  strength  which is out of all these diversities  that we have  that continues to be a strengthy family  system right so the more this  interaction increases  you know automatically your first level  of mental health intervention is  happening  sure so india's vastness is uh  in this case perhaps its strength dr  samir parikh from fortis healthcare has  been fascinating  here what you've had to say thanks for  joining us  thank you now it's time to answer  another  another of the questions you've been  sending into us today's  is 